  "behavior": [
    "Replace the raw iconv subject span and unbounded decoded-char vectors with a forbidunsafe streaming codec visitor and an owning original-runtime kernel. Size output first, admit complete source/output workspace before copying and retain each ticket with its actual Vec.",
    "Own arguments, selected source, attributes and original runtime pin across allocations, collection, argument detachment, callback panic and revocation. Copy attribute-list cells and preserve object/S4 flags; set encoding tags before constructor publication.",
    "Explicitly admit supported codec names; unknown source/target fail on the first nonmissing subject while empty/all-missing controls remain lazy. Honor list-of-raw/NULL input, raw-list output, NA/failure NULL, exact NUL restrictions and argument validation.",
    "Implement UTF16LE/BE and UTF32LE/BE with checked Rust Unicode primitives and integer wire representations. Preserve observed GNU extended UTF32-to-UTF8 bytes without invalid Rust chars/str. One sorted static codec table supplies advertised aliases without a native inventory Vec.",
    "Preserve GNU per-source-byte substitutions, Unicode/c99 policy and requested-spelling encoding marks. Keep existing portable transliteration table unchanged.",
    "Print malformed UTF8 as individual hex escapes while retaining valid scalar neighbors. Bound-check the historical GNU integer width decoder independently from the strict display decoder, preserving requested widths that differ from rendered escape length.",
    "Carry each matrix/array character field as text plus original width so invalid text survives as actual byte escapes, rather than NA, with faithful alignment."
  ],
