    "Old ASCII substitution fixture expected one ? for UTF8 \u00e9. Actual GNU substitutes each source byte, yielding two; corrected the expected value using the independent35-case contract.",
    "Initial i686 encoder fixture assumed UTF8 host locale; Miri default native-C returned9 rather than26. Preserve that failure, assert both native profiles, and unconditionally check the explicit GNU UTF8 width path. The later GNU width investigation established12 requested columns versus26 displayed columns for the malformed marked string, so retain that exact historical distinction.",
    "Intermediate valid conversion produced exact extended UTF8 bytes, but public rendering replaced them. Preserve the original35-case golden and fix the native printer; expanded6-case oracle exposes matrix/array and width behavior."
